A crashed server loses timers that existed only in memory. Decide whether to restore scheduled work and identify its durable recovery data.

Book basis: [B3](/lore/durability-bibliography#b3-designing-elixir-systems-with-otp).

## Failure it prevents

A scheduler restarts but pending deadlines silently disappear.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`DurableClock` and `DurableDeferred` cooperate with `WorkflowEngine`. For an existing storage/alarm owner, keep scheduling in that [adapter](/lore/hexagonal-architecture). A `Schedule` loop alone is not persistence.

Source: `packages/effect/src/workflow/DurableClock.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/DurableDeferred.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/WorkflowEngine.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Schedule.ts`.

## How to check

Crash before the deadline. Recover it from storage and test both wakeup and cancellation. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Durable work needs storage](/lore/durable-work-needs-storage), [Restart must reconstruct known state](/lore/restart-from-known-state).

Connect this to [the existing rat-stack guidance](/lore/lifecycles-are-machines).

